WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.607
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:08.131
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.431 --> 00:00:13.939
Unit four: Work-Life Balance. Today you will use gerunds after prepositions.

4
00:00:14.239 --> 00:00:16.787
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:20.862
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:22.811
Overload.

7
00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:26.165
Overload means too much work at one time.

8
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.098
Exam week is always an overload.

9
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:32.301
Your turn. Say: Overload.

10
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.319
Overload.

11
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:38.061
Time off.

12
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:42.002
Time off means time when you rest from work or study.

13
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:45.092
I take time off on Sunday afternoons.

14
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:48.138
Your turn. Say: Time off.

15
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.908
Time off.

16
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.837
Boundary setting.

17
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:58.127
Boundary setting means deciding clear limits on your time.

18
00:00:58.717 --> 00:01:00.797
Boundary setting protects my sleep.

19
00:01:01.383 --> 00:01:03.873
Your turn. Say: Boundary setting.

20
00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.036
Boundary setting.

21
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:09.901
Productivity.

22
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.427
Productivity means how much useful work you do.

23
00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:16.225
Short breaks increase productivity.

24
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.666
Your turn. Say: Productivity.

25
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.606
Productivity.

26
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.665
Burnout prevention.

27
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:30.739
Burnout prevention means stopping extreme tiredness before it starts.

28
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.559
Sleep is the best burnout prevention.

29
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.872
Your turn. Say: Burnout prevention.

30
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:41.361
Burnout prevention.

31
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:43.431
Self-discipline.

32
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:48.076
Self-discipline means controlling yourself to do what is needed.

33
00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:51.658
Self-discipline helps me finish homework early.

34
00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.158
Your turn. Say: Self-discipline.

35
00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.465
Self-discipline.

36
00:02:00.217 --> 00:02:01.508
Flexible schedule.

37
00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:05.468
Flexible schedule means a timetable that can change.

38
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:08.536
A flexible schedule lets me help at home.

39
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.011
Your turn. Say: Flexible schedule.

40
00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.228
Flexible schedule.

41
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:18.101
Priorities.

42
00:02:19.117 --> 00:02:22.068
Priorities means the most important things to do first.

43
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:25.136
My health and studies are my priorities.

44
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.379
Your turn. Say: Priorities.

45
00:02:31.233 --> 00:02:32.397
Priorities.

46
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.070
Downtime.

47
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:38.128
Downtime means time to relax and do nothing busy.

48
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:40.774
Everyone needs some downtime.

49
00:02:41.383 --> 00:02:44.047
Your turn. Say: Downtime.

50
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.901
Downtime.

51
00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.570
Recharge.

52
00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:52.838
Recharge means to get your energy back.

53
00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.693
I recharge by walking by the river.

54
00:02:56.283 --> 00:02:58.727
Your turn. Say: Recharge.

55
00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:02.545
Recharge.

56
00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.039
Sustainable pace.

57
00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:09.408
Sustainable pace means a speed you can keep for a long time.

58
00:03:10.017 --> 00:03:13.328
Study at a sustainable pace, not all night.

59
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:16.871
Your turn. Say: Sustainable pace.

60
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:21.315
Sustainable pace.

61
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.028
Wellness.

62
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:26.759
Wellness means being healthy in body and mind.

63
00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.048
Our school has a wellness week.

64
00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.674
Your turn. Say: Wellness.

65
00:03:35.533 --> 00:03:36.616
Wellness.

66
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.795
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.950
Visal, how do you balance schoolwork with personal time?

68
00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:50.908
I'm good at managing time. I set boundaries after nine p.m.

69
00:03:52.017 --> 00:03:53.830
What do you do in your downtime?

70
00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:59.032
I'm interested in playing football. It helps me recharge.

71
00:04:00.117 --> 00:04:01.919
And during exam overload?

72
00:04:03.017 --> 00:04:07.501
I focus on studying, but I'm careful about getting enough sleep.

73
00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.190
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.466
Grammar focus: Gerunds after prepositions.

75
00:04:14.766 --> 00:04:16.034
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.320
I focus on studying.

77
00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:20.972
I am good at managing time.

78
00:04:21.883 --> 00:04:23.720
She is tired of staying up late.

79
00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:28.988
After a preposition, always use the -ing form, never 'to' + verb.

80
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:33.111
Be careful! Don't say: I focus on study.

81
00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:37.171
Say: I focus on studying.

82
00:04:37.471 --> 00:04:40.155
After a preposition, use the -ing form.

83
00:04:40.967 --> 00:04:43.805
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.089
Finding My Balance.

85
00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:49.584
Last term, homework overload made me tired and stressed.

86
00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.830
Now I am good at setting boundaries and keeping priorities.

87
00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:58.795
Setting boundaries prevents burnout and keeps a sustainable pace.

88
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:03.216
Taking time off and recharging is as important as productivity.

89
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.012
I look forward to relaxing every Sunday afternoon.

90
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:12.079
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:12.917 --> 00:05:14.556
I am good at blank time.

92
00:05:14.856 --> 00:05:18.487
A, managing. B, manage. C, to manage.

93
00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:23.824
The answer is A: managing.

94
00:05:24.983 --> 00:05:27.587
Time to relax and do nothing busy is blank.

95
00:05:27.887 --> 00:05:31.749
A, downtime. B, overload. C, productivity.

96
00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.381
The answer is A: downtime.

97
00:05:38.517 --> 00:05:40.563
To get your energy back is to blank.

98
00:05:40.863 --> 00:05:45.329
A, recharge. B, overload. C, prioritize.

99
00:05:48.867 --> 00:05:51.400
The answer is A: recharge.

100
00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.554
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:56.417 --> 00:05:59.055
How do you balance schoolwork with personal time?

102
00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.397
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:09.697 --> 00:06:17.690
I am good at planning my week. After finishing my homework, I relax by reading or playing badminton with friends.

104
00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.769
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:20.683 --> 00:06:25.054
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and gerunds after prepositions.

106
00:06:25.354 --> 00:06:29.829
Today's value is balance. Enjoy screens a little, then play and read too.

107
00:06:30.129 --> 00:06:32.747
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

108
00:06:33.047 --> 00:06:35.838
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

